{%- comment -%}
  Line-item discount display — shared by the cart (`cart-item-price.liquid`) and
  the order/account page (`sections/main-order.liquid`).

  Renders real money discounts as compact tags and never prints a −₹0.00 amount.
  Background: some automatic discounts (e.g. a Buy-X-Get-Y promo) attach a ₹0
  allocation to the qualifying lines, which would otherwise show a verbose,
  meaningless "… −₹0.00" tag on an item the shopper is fully paying for.

  The visible label is shortened to the REWARD only — "₹300 Off", not
  "₹300 Off — Spend ₹3000" — because the qualifying condition is both already met
  and restated by the reward ladder. The full title and exact amount stay
  available to assistive tech and as the element's title attribute.

  Styled by assets/line-discounts.css, loaded globally from layout/theme.liquid.
  The CSS cannot live in a {% stylesheet %} block here: Shopify only compiles those
  for sections and blocks, so in a snippet it is silently never served and the 12px
  icon expands to fill its container.

  @param {object} item - a cart line item OR an order line item (both expose
                         line_level_discount_allocations, final_line_price,
                         properties).
  @param {boolean} force_inr - order history is a record of an INR charge, so
                         main-order passes true to keep every figure INR even
                         for a US-context visitor. Cart surfaces omit it.

  @example
  {% render 'line-discounts', item: item %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Skip lines that are actually free (the green FREE badge in cart-item-price owns
  them) and carousel gift lines. For paid lines, render only real money discounts —
  a ₹0 allocation artifact (the BXGY "buy"-side) is suppressed entirely, so there's
  never a "−₹0.00" or a stray freebie chip on an item the shopper is paying for.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign is_free_line = false
  if item.final_line_price == 0 and item.original_line_price > 0
    assign is_free_line = true
  elsif item.properties['_free_gift'] != blank
    assign is_free_line = true
  endif

  assign real_count = 0
  if is_free_line == false
    for allocation in item.line_level_discount_allocations
      if allocation.amount > 0
        assign real_count = real_count | plus: 1
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{%- if real_count > 0 -%}
  <ul class="discounts discounts--line list-unstyled" role="list" aria-label="{{ 'customer.order.discount' | t | escape }}">
    {%- for allocation in item.line_level_discount_allocations -%}
      {%- if allocation.amount > 0 -%}
        {%- liquid
          comment
            Admin names these discounts for the merchant's benefit — "₹300 Off —
            Spend ₹3000". In a cart line that is far too long for the narrow
            details column: it truncated mid-word and then wrapped the orphaned
            tail onto its own line. Everything after the dash is the QUALIFYING
            condition, which the shopper has by definition already met, and the
            reward ladder above states it anyway. Keep only the reward.
          endcomment
          assign disc_title = allocation.discount_application.title
          assign disc_short = disc_title | split: '—' | first
          assign disc_short = disc_short | split: '–' | first
          assign disc_short = disc_short | split: ' - ' | first
          assign disc_short = disc_short | strip

          comment
            These titles already name their amount, so printing it again beside
            them just says "₹300 Off  −₹300". Show the amount only when the title
            does not already carry it (a "Bundle deal" style discount).

            The test has to be on a WORD boundary. `contains` is a substring
            match, and allocation.amount is this LINE's share, not the whole
            discount: a ₹300 order-class discount spread over lines gives a ₹30
            allocation, and "₹300 Off" contains "₹30" — so the amount was
            suppressed and the row rendered a bare "₹300 Off" on a line that had
            actually received ₹30. Appending a space to both sides makes "₹30 "
            fail against "₹300 Off " while "₹300 " still matches.
          endcomment
          assign disc_amount = allocation.amount | money_without_trailing_zeros
          assign disc_probe = disc_amount | append: ' '
          assign disc_haystack = disc_short | append: ' '
          assign disc_shows_amount = false
          if disc_haystack contains disc_probe
            assign disc_shows_amount = true
          endif

          comment
            US context: every printed surface — the visible pill, the title
            tooltip and the sr-only sentence — converts its ladder figures to
            USD via usd-inr-text. This runs AFTER the suppression probe above,
            which must keep comparing INR strings: Admin titles are INR-worded.
          endcomment
          if force_inr
            assign disc_short_display = disc_short
            assign disc_title_display = disc_title
            capture disc_amount_display
              echo allocation.amount | money
            endcapture
          else
            capture disc_short_display
              render 'usd-inr-text', text: disc_short
            endcapture
            capture disc_title_display
              render 'usd-inr-text', text: disc_title
            endcapture
            capture disc_amount_display
              render 'money-display', amount: allocation.amount
            endcapture
          endif
        -%}
        <li class="discounts__discount" title="{{ disc_title_display | escape }}">
          <svg class="discounts__icon" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2.5 7.6V3.3a.8.8 0 0 1 .8-.8h4.3a.8.8 0 0 1 .57.24l5.3 5.3a.8.8 0 0 1 0 1.13l-4.3 4.3a.8.8 0 0 1-1.13 0l-5.3-5.3a.8.8 0 0 1-.24-.57Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"/><circle cx="5.6" cy="5.6" r="1" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
          <span class="discounts__title">{{ disc_short_display }}</span>
          {%- unless disc_shows_amount -%}
            <span class="discounts__amount">&minus;{{ disc_amount_display }}</span>
          {%- endunless -%}
          <span class="sr-only">, {{ disc_title_display | escape }}, &minus;{{ disc_amount_display }}</span>
        </li>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
{%- endif -%}
